# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# PlatformIO build output (tools/espnow-sniffer)
.pio/

# Python bytecode (tools/beacons)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Captures. `wartui run` writes `wartui-<date>.db` to the working directory unless
# `--db` says otherwise, so the repository root is where one lands if you run it
# from here — and a capture is a list of the access points around whoever ran it,
# which is the one thing in this project that must never be committed.
# A `.db` or `.pcap` anywhere in this tree is a capture by definition, so those
# are unanchored. A `.csv` is not — an export-regression fixture would be a
# reasonable thing to check in — so two narrower rules cover the exports: the
# working directory, and a capture's own name anywhere beneath it, since
# `wartui export` writes beside the capture under that name unless told otherwise.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.pcap
/*.csv
wartui-*.csv

# macOS
.DS_Store

# AI tools
.claude/worktrees
